<title>USA: Ibah Q4 profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Ibah Q4 profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>BLUE BELL, Pa. 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>IBAH INC AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>	   (all amounts in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>			    For the Three Months  For the Full Year</p>
<p>			     Ended December 31,  Ended December 31,</p>
<p>			     1996	   1995	1996	 1995</p>
<p> Revenues		$26,625     $17,155   $82,609    $56,985</p>
<p>Less: Reimbursed costs</p>
<p>			     6,151	 5,129    20,453     14,119</p>
<p> Net revenues	   20,474	12,026    62,156     42,866</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>  Direct		   9,556	 6,125    30,960     23,847</p>
<p>Selling, general</p>
<p>and administrative</p>
<p>			    10,004	 6,091    30,121     21,921</p>
<p>Acquired research</p>
<p>   and development (A)   ---	   ---	 510	  ---</p>
<p>Operating profit (loss) from:</p>
<p>  Continuing Operations  914	 (190)	 565    (2,902)</p>
<p>Interest income</p>
<p>   (expense), net	  176	    11	 475	(111)</p>
<p>Income (loss) from</p>
<p>continuing operations</p>
<p>			     1,090	 (179)     1,040    (3,013)</p>
<p>Loss from discontinued</p>
<p>   operations (B)	  ---	 (417)	 ---    (1,546)</p>
<p>Income (loss)</p>
<p>before income taxes</p>
<p>			     1,090	 (596)     1,040    (4,559)</p>
<p>  Income taxes		60	   ---	  60	  ---</p>
<p>  Net income(loss)     1,030	 (596)	 980    (4,559)</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per share:</p>
<p>Continuing operations</p>
<p>				0.04	(0.01)	0.04     (0.21)</p>
<p>Discontinued operations ---</p>
<p>					    (0.03)	 ---     (0.11)</p>
<p>				0.04	(0.04)	0.04     (0.32)</p>
<p>Shares outstanding (C)</p>
<p>			    27,984	14,360    24,997     14,276</p>
<p>(A) Represents a portion of the purchase price for Resource Biometrics, Inc. acquired in July 1996 allocated to research activities.  </p>
<p>(B) Discontinued operations represents the operating results of Drug Delivery Services which was divested in July 1995.</p>
<p>(C) Represents the weighted number of shares outstanding; for 1996, the shares outstanding represent the weighted number of outstanding shares and common stock equivalents.</p>
<p>Net profit before a one-time charge to earnings related to the acquisition of RBI was $1.5 million or $.06 per share as compared to a loss of $3.0 million in 1995 from continuing operations or a loss of $.21 per share.</p>
<p>For full 1996, net profit after a one-time charge related to the acquisition of RBI was $1.0 million or $.04 per share in 1996, as compared to a loss in 1995, inclusive of discontinued operations, of $4.6 million, or $.32 per share.</p>
